    ["In how many genera are distributed the 2 500 known cacti species?", "90", "Systematically, genus is a taxonomic rank that groups together a set of species that share similar characteristics.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_224.json", null, false, "medium", ["30", "50", "90", "70"]],
    ["What young artist sang 'Jour de neige' on television in 1988?", "Elsa", "The producers have accompanied the single of this most rhythmic title of the club version album intended for discotheques.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_186.json", null, false, "easy", ["Patricia Kaas", "Elsa", "Lio", "Jakie Quartz"]],
    ["How fast can a peregrine falcon reach when it is on its prey?", "240 km / h", "Its prey is often birds, but some individuals can also attack small land animals.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_175.json", null, false, "medium", ["120 km / h", "200 km / h", "240 km / h", "160 km / h"]],
    ["What does the word “ski” mean in Norwegian, where does its origin come from?", "Bûche", "In Norwegian, the word “ski” would mean “piece of wood” because the skis of the time were cut in the wood with axes.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_186.json", null, false, "medium", ["Hoof", "Bûche", "Boot", "Concrete"]],
    ["Which Russian volcano woke up after 250 years of deep sleep?", "Kambalny", "A minor eruption of the Kambalny volcano took place in 1767 but the last major eruption was around 600 years ago.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_199.json", null, false, "medium", ["Ketoï", "Kolumbo", "Kurub", "Kambalny"]],
    ["Which active volcano is the highest in Europe with 3 330 meters of altitude?", "Etna", "Its relatively steep slopes are interrupted by several eruptions, especially on its southern and western flanks.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_199.json", null, false, "easy", ["Etna", "Ebeko", "Olca", "Mount Fuji"]],
    ["What is a person who raises honey bees called?", "Beekeeper", "Practiced on all continents, this activity differs according to bee varieties, climate and economic development.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_237.json", null, false, "medium", ["Raniculteur", "Poultry farmer", "Oyster farmer", "Beekeeper"]],
    ["What food does the horse really appreciate?", "Oats", "Oats are straw cereals and are widely used in animal feed (especially from equine).", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_173.json", null, false, "easy", ["Fodder", "Hay", "Oats", "Muesli"]],
    ["In general, how many hours a day is a giant panda busy eating?", "Sixteen", "The giant panda eats only young bamboo shoots but these are not very nutritious.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_184.json", null, false, "hard", ["Twelve", "Four", "Sixteen", "Eight"]],
    ["Who wrote the French novel 'La neige en deuil' offered to many students?", "Henri Troyat", "This fiction (and the film) is inspired by a real event: the accident of the Malabar Princess on the flanks of Mont Blanc in 1950.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_186.json", null, false, "medium", ["Jean Vautrin", "Jean-Paul Sartre", "Henri Troyat", "Bernard Clavel"]],
    ["The eruption of what volcano caused on Earth a general cooling of 0.6°C?", "Pinatubo", "The human toll, which amounts to less than 1 000 deaths, was relatively limited thanks to the effective evacuation of the populations.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_199.json", null, false, "medium", ["Pinatubo", "Rasshua", "Misti", "Kurub"]],
    ["Which forest hill is located on the eastern edge of Lake Bourget?", "Corsuet Forest", "The Corsuet forest and its hiking trails are managed by the agglomeration community of Lake Bourget.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_203.json", null, false, "medium", ["Corsuet Forest", "Lorge Forest", "Brotonne Forest", "Forest of Dourdan"]],
    ["How many milliliters of blood can a vampire bat drink in one night?", "20 ml", "The vampire bat is native to the tropical areas of the American continent (Mexico, Chile, Brazil and Argentina).", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_175.json", null, false, "medium", ["60 ml", "20 ml", "80 ml", "40 ml"]],
    ["What substance is often used to quickly melt snow on roads?", "Salt", "In France, roads are classified into four levels of priority, with level 1 roads being treated 24 hours a day if necessary.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_186.json", null, false, "easy", ["Flour", "Pepper", "Salt", "Sugar"]],
    ["In which maternity of the hive develop the future bees?", "Couvain", "It is generally located in the center of the hive and is surrounded by honeycombs and pollen (bee bread) to feed it.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_237.json", null, false, "hard", ["Levant", "Couvain", "Beaker", "Dormitory"]],
    ["What part of the body allows seahorses to swim?", "Dorsal fin", "Although they are fish, seahorses swim very slowly with wavy movements.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_184.json", null, false, "easy", ["Dorsal fin", "Head", "Ventral fin", "Tail"]],
    ["What name does the V-shaped protrusion stand under the horse's foot?", "The fork", "The horse's fork is a protruding V-shaped projection with a softer tubular horn.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_173.json", null, false, "hard", ["The corner", "The punch", "The bead", "The fork"]],
    ["What equipment is required to take the start of a ski descent competition?", "Helmet", "The descent is the oldest sport of alpine skiing, now called the discipline queen of its category.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_186.json", null, false, "easy", ["Knee pads", "Brassard", "Helmet", "Glasses"]],
    ["What little bee delighted children on television in the 1980s?", "Maya", "Maya discovers the world in the company of her friends Willy the bee, Flip the grasshopper, Max the earthworm and Alexander the mouse.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_237.json", null, false, "easy", ["Heidi", "Zigby", "Maya", "Tao Tao"]],
    ["At what age must a pigeon intended for competition be ringed?", "8-9 days", "If the youngster is too large, it is indeed no longer possible to pass the ring to the leg, the latter having a precise diameter.", "Damien Moreau · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_413.json", null, false, "medium", ["8-9 days", "2 months", "1 year", "25-26 days"]],
    ["In Europe, what is the first flower that usually grows at the end of winter?", "Crocus", "With its large purple flower, Crocus sativus, from which saffron is extracted, needs a lot of heat to bloom.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_186.json", null, false, "easy", ["Ficus", "Acacia", "Dahlia", "Crocus"]],
    ["Where are your feet positioned when riding?", "Stirrups", "To erect it would be a Chinese invention, while for others it would come from the nomadic peoples of Central Asia or Siberia.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_173.json", null, false, "easy", ["Reines", "Stirrups", "Straps", "Baudriers"]],
    ["Which state forest is the largest in the department of Finistere?", "Cranou Forest", "The Cranou Forest was exploited for the timber needs of the Royal Navy in Brest, the logs being transported via the port of Faou.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_203.json", null, false, "medium", ["Montfort Forest", "Forest of Grésigne", "Bonifatu Forest", "Cranou Forest"]],
    ["Which animals often steal from hyenas the prey they have hunted?", "Lions", "Hyenas usually hunt in packs of about forty individuals of animals such as zebras or wildebeest.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_184.json", null, false, "medium", ["Buffalo", "Lions", "Wildebeest", "Guards"]],
    ["How long after birth does a foal walk?", "Immediately", "This peculiarity is inherited from their ancestors the wild horses that were the prey of many predators.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_173.json", null, false, "easy", ["After 4 weeks", "After a month", "Immediately", "After 2 weeks"]],
    ["How much does a normally formed mosquito have teeth?", "47", "Adults feed on flower nectar and participate in the pollination of plants, just like butterflies.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_175.json", null, false, "hard", ["34", "47", "29", "11"]],
    ["With what part of her body does the mole move under the ground?", "Vibrisses", "The moles orient themselves almost exclusively by using a kind of mustache and kill their food in this way.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_184.json", null, false, "medium", ["Muzzle", "Ears", "Eyes", "Vibrisses"]],
    ["What gray volcano is on the Sino-Korean border?", "Mount Paektu", "Its summit is occupied by a vast caldera 5 km in diameter and 850 m deep, partially filled by the lake of Paradise.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_199.json", null, false, "hard", ["Mount Paektu", "Mount Taranaki", "Wrangell Mountain", "Mount Tongariro"]],
    ["Which comic strip is particularly devoted to pigeon racing?", "The old blue", "This 1974 comic, famous in the pigeon sport, was drawn by François Walthéry and scripted by Raoul Cauvin.", "Damien Moreau · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_413.json", null, false, "hard", ["The old blue", "The pigeon sport", "Colombo Phil", "The carrier pigeon"]],
    ["How many days does an Alaskan squirrel hibernate?", "270 days", "The squirrel's plume tail and its relentless winter provisions have contributed to its popularity.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_175.json", null, false, "hard", ["180 days", "270 days", "320 days", "410 days"]],
    ["What Nordic people owe, among other things, the invention of sledding?", "Vikings", "It seems that the Vikings already used sleds with two skates at that time, much like the current sleds.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_186.json", null, false, "medium", ["Celts", "Scottish", "Romans", "Vikings"]],
    ["Why can not we hear the cries of the bat?", "Too acute", "The bats emit and receive ultrasounds that our ear can not perceive (max 20 000 hertz).", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_184.json", null, false, "easy", ["Too weak", "Too strong", "Too serious", "Too acute"]],
    ["What position do horses adopt for a light sleep?", "Standing", "Like most large herbivores, the horse sleeps little (3 to 5 hours a day) because of its vulnerability to predators.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_173.json", null, false, "easy", ["On the right flank", "On the left flank", "On the belly", "Standing"]],
    ["What is the name of the winged horse of Greek mythology?", "Pegasus", "Pegasus ascends to heaven after his birth and puts himself at the service of Zeus who charges him with bringing lightning to Olympus.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_173.json", null, false, "easy", ["Fungus", "Argus", "Merengo", "Pegasus"]],
    ["Which is the largest artificial forest in Western Europe?", "Forest of the Landes", "Bordered by the Atlantic Ocean, the forest of the Lande forms a vast triangle covering three departments (Gironde, Landes and Lot-et-Garonne).", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_203.json", null, false, "easy", ["Forest of the Landes", "Benon Forest", "Creuse Forest", "Forest of Chevrè"]],
    ["What do bees do flying from flower to flower in search of food?", "They are foraging", "The bee harvests in nature nectar, propolis, honeydew and pollen.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_237.json", null, false, "easy", ["They draw", "They skate", "They ruminate", "They are foraging"]],
    ["What does the phrase 'not to be under the hoof of a horse' mean?", "To be rare", "Originally, in the seventeenth century, the expression contained 'in the step of a horse', the step wanting to mean the word 'trace'.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_173.json", null, false, "medium", ["To be fast", "To be stingy", "Be careful", "To be rare"]],
    ["What important phenomenon does the bee provide by foraging?", "Pollination", "Plants contribute to the diet of pollinators by providing them with excess pollen or nectar.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_237.json", null, false, "easy", ["Germination", "Pollination", "Introgression", "Sporulation"]],
    ["Ideally, how often is it necessary to repot a cactus?", "Every 4 years", "The cactuses do not like the excess of food, the cactus will grow if the volume of the pot does not exceed that of the plant.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_224.json", null, false, "medium", ["Every 16 years", "Every 12 years", "Every 8 years", "Every 4 years"]],
    ["Which Austrian city crossed by the Inn is the capital of Tyrol?", "Innsbruck", "Innsbruck is the fifth largest city in Austria from the point of view of the population, after Vienna, Graz, Linz and Salzburg.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_186.json", null, false, "medium", ["Vienna", "Innsbruck", "Graz", "Salzburg"]],
    ["What have replaced Napoleon Bonaparte's imperial bees?", "Lily flower", "The golden fleur-de-lis on the azure field became the arms of France and the specific emblem of the kings of France.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_237.json", null, false, "hard", ["Myosotis", "Blueberry", "Lily flower", "Clover"]],
    ["Which Italian volcano at an altitude of 1,281 meters borders the Bay of Naples?", "Vesuvius", "Vesuvius is at the origin of the destruction of the cities of Pompeii, Herculaneum, Oplontis and Stabies, buried on August 24, 79.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_199.json", null, false, "easy", ["Vesuvius", "Stromboli", "Pinatubo", "Villarrica"]],
    ["Which volcano is located in the Big Ben volcanic massif?", "Mawson Peak", "The Mawson Peak is in the form of a stratovolcano rising in the heart of the caldera, Australia.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_199.json", null, false, "hard", ["Mawson Peak", "Baratang", "Nazko Cone", "Mount Gharat"]],
    ["How much light does a cactus need to flourish?", "The maximum", "However, after wintering, do not expose your cacti directly in direct sunlight but prefer a gradual return to light.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_224.json", null, false, "easy", ["Many", "None", "The maximum", "A little"]],
    ["Which honey bee is the product of the hatching of an unfertilized egg?", "False drone", "Unlike the female worker bee, the drone has no stinger and does not harvest nectar or pollen.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_237.json", null, false, "easy", ["False drone", "Stick insect", "Tick", "Beetle"]],
    ["Which volcano of the United States is the highest volcano in the world?", "Mauna Loa", "The Mauna Loa is 17 kilometers above its base, which sinks into the ocean floor.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_199.json", null, false, "medium", ["Vanua Lava", "Marapi", "Tecapa", "Mauna Loa"]],
    ["Which African general crossed the Alps with elephants?", "Hannibal", "Most of Hannibal's 27 elephants actually died in the Alps crossing or in the wetness of the marshlands.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_186.json", null, false, "easy", ["Didon", "Hannon", "Hannibal", "Hasdrubal"]],
    ["How many eggs does the female pigeon usually lay per clutch?", "Two", "If, for example, the eggs are broken, the female usually lays again after about ten days.", "Damien Moreau · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_413.json", null, false, "medium", ["Eight", "Two", "Six", "Four"]],
    ["Who is the only fertile female individual in a bee colony?", "Queen", "The queen, with a more elongated abdomen, is usually the mother of most, if not all, bees in the hive.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_237.json", null, false, "easy", ["Worker", "Queen", "Wasp", "Hornet"]],
    ["How do sowbugs protect themselves from attacks?", "By wrapping up", "The body of a woodlouse, in this case immobile, is composed of several solid rings that recall a knight's armor.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_184.json", null, false, "medium", ["By wrapping up", "By burying himself", "In flight", "By flying away"]],
    ["What part of the body of the slug does it allow to cut the plants?", "Language", "Like a file, the slug's sluggish tongue grows the tender plants into small pieces and thus strips the young salads.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_184.json", null, false, "easy", ["Palace", "Bras", "Teeth", "Language"]],
    ["Which volcano in Papua New Guinea is also called The Father?", "Ulawun", "The Ulawun volcano is subject to an equatorial climate that allows the establishment of a humid tropical forest.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_199.json", null, false, "hard", ["Teahitia", "Ulawun", "Mount Usu", "Visoke"]],
    ["Which forest is located on a butte-witness dominating the plain of France?", "Carnelle Forest", "Among its fauna are deer, wild boar or deer from the forest of Chantilly, foxes, badgers and rabbits.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_203.json", null, false, "hard", ["Forest of Gâvre", "Chantilly Forest", "Paimpont Forest", "Carnelle Forest"]],
    ["Who wrote the new title 'Les neiges du Kilimandjaro'?", "Hemingway", "The news published in 1936 was translated in France by Marcel Duhamel and adapted to the film under the same title by Henry King.", "Philippe Bresoux · OpenQuizzDB.org (CC BY-SA 4.0)", "https://github.com/Zeuh/OpenQuizzDB/blob/a16819964d171e40e6652368fc562f3bd27d0c5b/data/openquizzdb_186.json", null, false, "medium", ["Mauriac", "Camus", "Steinbeck", "Hemingway"]]
